WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.920
Start in the installed SOCpilot environment, run the policy example and save its output.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:10.080
This synthetic incident proposes two actions.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.480
The first rebuilds the host, the second isolates it.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.480
The example declares two rules.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:22.420
An investigator must collect evidence before rebuilding the host.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:26.440
For this incident, the policy also prohibits isolation.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.440
The checker reports both violations.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.740
The plan schedules the rebuild before collecting evidence.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.240
The proposed isolation also violates the second rule.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:43.000
Follow the edits back to the proposal.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:48.900
The repair removes isolation and inserts forensic collection before rebuilding.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.880
The resulting sequence is visible in the same output file.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.520
Finally, inspect the verdict on the repaired plan.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.760
The violations list is empty.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.100
A second repair leaves the sequence unchanged.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:09.420
This checks a plan against the declared policy before anyone acts on the host.
